.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Emmy Noether&#x27;s theorem ties each continuous symmetry of a system&#x27;s action to an exactly conserved quantity built from it: time-translation symmetry gives energy, rotational symmetry gives angular momentum. The Kepler problem carries a third, less obvious conserved quantity, the Laplace-Runge-Lenz vector">

