.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="The three animation helpers in physicskit.classical.visualizers.animations and physicskit.classical.visualizers.modal_analysis, applied to three already-familiar conservative systems, each paired with a live diagnostic of its own governing physics: a double pendulum (~physicskit.classical.systems.lagrangian.DoublePendulum, governed by its Euler-Lagrange equations of motion) shown with its physical rods next to a growing (\theta_1, \dot\theta_1) phase trace; a precessing Kepler orbit (~physicskit.classical.systems.newtonian.KeplerSystem, whose post-Newtonian term c_\mathrm{pn}/r^3 in V(r) drives the precession) shown with its orbital path next to a growing energy trace; and a non-linear lattice chain (~physicskit.classical.systems.chains.FPUTChain) shown via its live modal-energy bar chart E_k(t).">

